{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{artist: Thomas O. Chisholm / William M. Runyan}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening, Response}
{key: D}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
# Published 1923; in the US public domain since 2019.

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Great is Thy [G]faith[D]fulness, O [A7]God my Fa[D]ther
There is no [G]shadow of [D]turning with [A7]Thee
Thou [D]changest not, Thy [G]compassions, they [D]fail [Bm]not
As Thou [Em]hast been Thou for[A7]ever wilt [D]be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Great is Thy [G]faithfulness! [D]Great is Thy [Bm]faithfulness!
[Em]Morning by [D]morning new [A7]mercies I [D]see
All I have [G]needed Thy [D]hand hath pro[Bm]vided
[Em]Great is Thy [D/F#]faithfulness, [A7]Lord, unto [D]me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Summer and [G]winter, and [D]springtime and [A7]harvest
[D]Sun, moon and [G]stars in their [D]courses a[A7]bove
Join with [D]all nature in [G]manifold [D]wit[Bm]ness
To Thy [Em]great faithful[A7]ness, mercy and [D]love
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Pardon for [G]sin and a [D]peace that en[A7]dureth
Thine own [D]dear presence to [G]cheer and to [D]guide [A7]
[D]Strength for to[G]day and bright [D]hope for to[Bm]morrow
[Em]Blessings all [A7]mine, with ten [D]thousand be[A7]side[D]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
